text:
GENERATE BURST SO-1 — Run C-9 (Matt R-C9-80): a second character for the same world as the Norse barbarian already built, a FIRE SORCERESS: her BASE BODY as a CHARACTER SHEET for a 3D model. task_id "SO-1".

WHY this sheet exists (so you can judge your own result): a 3D model will be built from these four views, then rigged and animated. Her robe, mantle, circlet, bracers and staff will be added LATER as separate pieces on top of this body. So this sheet shows her with the LEAST clothing and gear, and the four views must agree exactly, as four views of ONE body.

IMAGE 1 is a STYLE reference ONLY. Copy its HAND: the warm dark-brown ink line that varies in weight, the transparent watercolor washes that pool, granulate and bloom, the fine hatching in the shadows, the cream paper highlights, the warm moderate colour. Copy NOTHING else from it: not its character, face, hair, hood, robe, staff, bag, pose or clothing colours. She is a DIFFERENT person from the figure in IMAGE 1 and must not resemble it.

THE CHARACTER, a fire sorceress of the North, base body:
- a tall, lean, strong woman of about thirty: long-limbed and athletic, a fighter's build rather than a model's; natural proportions, about seven and a half heads tall;
- dressed ONLY in a plain sleeveless knee-length SHIFT of undyed grey-cream linen, fitted enough to show the body's shape, with a plain dark leather BELT at the waist and a small bronze buckle; nothing hangs from the belt;
- bare arms; pale skin with faint freckles across the shoulders; ONE band of angular runic tattoos in ember-orange ink around her LEFT forearm only (her right arm is bare);
- straight BLACK hair: shaved short at the LEFT temple, the rest bound into ONE thick braid that hangs straight down her back to between the shoulder blades, with a small bronze ring at its end;
- soft dark leather BOOTS to mid-calf with clear toes;
- NOTHING ELSE: no robe, no cloak, no mantle, no fur, no hood, no circlet, no bracers, no jewellery except the braid ring, no staff, no orb, no wand, no bag, no pouch, no fire or glow;
- a calm, level face: mouth closed, eyes open, looking straight ahead.

SHEET: ONE 1024x1536 PORTRAIT sheet on flat pure #00ff00 in a 2x2 grid: the SAME woman in four views at the SAME scale, each view centred in its quarter, soles on one ground line per row, each figure filling most of its quarter's height. Top-left FRONT (facing the viewer); top-right her RIGHT SIDE (in profile, facing the viewer's right); bottom-left BACK (seen from behind); bottom-right her LEFT SIDE (in profile, facing the viewer's left).
POSE (for building and rigging a 3D model): a relaxed A-POSE. Both arms straight and held AWAY from the body at about 30 degrees, so that in the front and back views a clear gap of green shows between each arm and the torso. Hands OPEN: fingers together and straight, thumbs slightly apart, palms facing the thighs. Legs straight, feet a little apart and pointing forward, weight even. Head level, facing the same way as the body. The braid hangs straight down her back, clear of the arms. Nothing overlaps anything.
She must be ONE consistent woman in all four views: the same face, hair, braid, tattoo (on the LEFT forearm in every view where that arm shows), shift, belt and boots.
STYLE: the REGISTER CARD above governs line, washes, light and plate. Its manuscript-subject clause does not apply to this figure: her subject and costume are set by this brief (Matt R-C9-80). Paint her in IMAGE 1's hand. Soft even light; no cast shadows, no ground, no text, no labels, no cell borders, no other figures.

Two image_gen calls: variants a and b. ONE retry per variant only if a view is missing or has the wrong facing, the woman differs between views, an arm touches the torso in the front or back view, any robe, cloak, fur, jewellery beyond the braid ring, staff or other gear appears, the tattoo is on the wrong arm, or the background is not flat green — name the reason. Copy outputs to out/SO-1_a.png and out/SO-1_b.png with sha256. No code. No other files. No web.
RETURN: receipt task_id "SO-1"; images = the files with prompt, references (role + path) and elapsed_s; calls_used = the TRUE number of image_gen calls; status; concerns. Never PASS/FAIL.
